Design: the last literal numbers in the critique's spec

Four places where the built components drifted from the numbers the
vision critic wrote down, found by auditing each component against
design-critique-1.md section 4 rather than by re-reading the build.

- FooterColumns label was 10px (--ns-text-3xs); the spec says 11px.
  Moved to --ns-text-2xs.
- SegmentedControl ground used --ns-muted (paper-3/paper-4), one step
  darker than the spec's paper-2. --ns-surface is paper-2 in *both*
  themes, which is the well the active pill lifts out of: lighter than
  the card in light, darker than it in dark. A ramp step would have
  inverted on one theme, which is what T2a forbids.
- ComparisonAreaChart: the plot bleeds to the viewBox floor, so the
  18% fill painted square across the frame's 12px radius. Clip the
  <svg>, not the frame — the hover readout is absolutely positioned
  above the node and would have been cut off on a peak.
  The baseline rule was stroked centred on y=120, the exact viewBox
  edge, so half of it fell outside the viewport; draw it at 119.5.
- SemicircularGauge spoke a raw number in its aria-label and hardcoded
  the domain noun "run items" inside a generic ui/ component. It now
  takes totalDisplay — a preformatted string (H2) — and names the
  segments from their own display strings. Callers pass it.

103 passed, 0 failed. deno check, lint and fmt clean.
