Design: the provisional tag was the dark-mode bug again, and the gate missed it

provisional-tag.css reached for primitive --ns-amber-6, exactly the
failure the critique flagged on exception-badge. It shipped anyway.

The fallback hid it: `var(--ns-amber-6, var(--ns-status-refunded))`
never falls back, because the primitive is always defined in :root, so
the stylesheet reads as themed at a glance. It was not. The amber ramp
does not invert for dark, and --ns-status-progress correctly moves to
amber-4 there, so this one tag was *darker* on a dark card (5.43:1)
than the semantic it shadowed (9.74:1).

It also slipped the T2a gate because the pattern was anchored on `\),`
and a ramp step carrying a fallback ends in a comma. Tightened to
`\s*[,)]`, which catches both shapes and still passes semantic roles
and semantic fallbacks.

Now --ns-status-progress, which is the role a provisional figure
actually is: in flight.

103 passed, 0 failed.
EOF
