Design: a compact amount was the one figure whose currency went unstyled

Every amount on the page renders its symbol in `.ns-money__currency` —
0.75em, muted — except compact ones. The `compact` branch skipped
`moneyParts` entirely and rendered `formatMoneyCompact`'s single
concatenated string, so `$1.2M` printed the symbol at full hero size
and full contrast.

`formatMoneyCompact` could not simply be changed: chart ticks and dense
readouts take one string, and they want the symbol inline. So the split
is now the same split `moneyParts` already makes — added
`compactMoneyParts`, which returns currency and text separately, and
`formatMoneyCompact` is now built on top of it. The component's two
branches collapse into one render path, because they now agree on shape.

Sign stays in the text, so `-$12k` keeps the sign inside the
direction-coloured element rather than ahead of the symbol. Absent
shares one literal (`ABSENT_MONEY_PARTS`) with `moneyParts` instead of
being restated.

Test added for the split; 104 passed, 0 failed.
EOF
